Tarnvale: \(5,207\) megalitres \(= 5,207,000,000\) litres.

\[
\frac{5,207,000,000}{71,388 \times 365}
= \frac{5,207,000,000}{26,056,620}
= 199.756\ldots\text{ litres per resident per day}
\]

Ashgrove: \(4,390\) megalitres \(= 4,390,000,000\) litres.

\[
\frac{4,390,000,000}{58,760 \times 365}
= \frac{4,390,000,000}{21,447,400}
= 204.685\ldots\text{ litres per resident per day}
\]

\[
204.685\ldots - 199.756\ldots = 4.929\ldots
\]

Rounded only in the final line: Ashgrove used more water by \(4.929\) litres per resident per day.

ANSWER: Ashgrove | 4.929

